I think we should just use `Symbol.GetArity()` instead of pattern matching, and also test the analogous method case:

```cs
class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        // error CS0308: The non-generic method 'Program.M(object)' cannot be used with type arguments
        // (It seems reasonable to prefer `M<T1, T2>` in this case for the same reason as a type.)
        M<int>(default!); 
    }

    void M(object obj) { }
    T2 M<T1, T2>(T1 t) => throw null!;
}
```
